# WARN: issue with `defaults` is that it converts a plist to binary data, eg. when writing to it.

# 1. Read
# Retrieve the value of a key or nested key path.
#
# Optionally support reading multiple keys at once.
#
# Handle different plist domains or files.
#
# 2. Write / Set
# Add or update a key with a value.
#
# Support specifying the data type explicitly (string, bool, int, etc.).
#
# Support nested key paths, creating intermediate dictionaries if needed.
#
# 3. Delete / Remove
# Remove a key or nested key path from the plist.
#
# 4. List / Dump
# Show all keys and values in a plist, optionally with nested structure.
#
# Support output formatting (e.g., JSON, YAML, or plain key=value).
#
# 5. Toggle
# For boolean keys, toggle between true and false.
#
# Could extend to toggle integer keys between 0/1 or other common pairs.
#
# 6. Exists / Check
# Check if a given key or nested key exists.
#
# 7. Backup / Restore
# Create a backup copy of the plist before modifying.
#
# Restore from a backup.
#
# 8. Import / Export
# Import plist contents from JSON or XML.
#
# Export plist contents to JSON or XML.
#
# 9. Watch / Monitor (advanced)
# Watch a plist file for changes and react (useful for live reloading settings).
#
# | Operation     | Description                   | Typical Command Example                     |
# | ------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
# | Read          | Get key value                 | `plist-cli read com.example.key`            |
# | Write         | Set key value with type       | `plist-cli write com.example.key bool true` |
# | Delete        | Remove a key                  | `plist-cli delete com.example.key`          |
# | List/Dump     | List all keys and values      | `plist-cli list com.example`                |
# | Toggle        | Toggle boolean or 0/1 integer | `plist-cli toggle com.example.enabled`      |
# | Exists        | Check if key exists           | `plist-cli exists com.example.key`          |
# | Backup        | Backup plist                  | `plist-cli backup com.example`              |
# | Restore       | Restore plist backup          | `plist-cli restore com.example.bak`         |
# | Import/Export | Import/export JSON/XML        | `plist-cli import my.json`                  |

